1
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:23,200
Now commencing the
57th Exterior Scouting Mission!

2
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,540
Move out!

3
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:34,370
We believe that the basement of
Eren Jaeger's home in Shiganshina

4
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:38,370
houses a secret of the Titans
that not even <i>he </i>is aware of.

5
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:41,290
We are to head there.

6
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:43,500
You rookies will be here,

7
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:47,370
between the wagon defense
squad and the scout support squad.

8
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:51,000
Here, you will run alongside
spare horses and relay signals.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,080
Our special operations squad
will be positioned here,

10
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:56,120
on standby in the
rear of the center rank.

11
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:57,120
This is the safest position

12
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,870
"Row 5, Center: Standby"
in the formation.

13
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:02,540
Not even the supply wagons
get this level of treatment.

14
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,290
This isn't an Abnormal...

15
00:01:15,290 --> 00:01:17,700
--Cis!
--It has intelligence!

16
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:21,200
It's just like the Armored Titan,
the Colossal Titan, and Eren!

17
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,120
It's a human clad in a Titan body!

18
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:29,200
This one's <i>way </i>more
athletic than the other ones!

19
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,200
Damn! We were...

20
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,580
We were too naïve!

21
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,870
She's protecting her nape?!

22
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:38,870
Damn! There's no escape now!

23
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:42,830
Jean! Avenge that suicidal maniac!

24
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:46,330
She stopped?

25
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:49,080
It was her! She killed him!

26
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:51,910
That maniac finally got himself killed,
as part of the right wing!

27
00:01:51,910 --> 00:01:54,700
She killed him!

28
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,620
I'd say we bought enough time!

29
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:13,950
Now let's get
away from her, quick!

30
00:02:13,950 --> 00:02:16,250
Huh? Oh no...

31
00:02:16,250 --> 00:02:17,700
Why?

32
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:21,540
Is she heading for Eren?!

33
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:57,580
<i>I won't let your deaths be meaningless</i>

34
00:02:57,580 --> 00:03:03,700
<i>even if I'm the last one standing</i>

35
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:12,580
<i>In both hands, Gloria</i>

36
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:14,580
<i>What sings is Sieg</i>

37
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:19,790
<i>On my back, Flügel der Freiheit</i>

38
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:26,660
<i>Clenched determination to my left chest</i>

39
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:32,000
<i>What slashes across is Linie der Torheit</i>

40
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:35,250
<i>Soaring across the azure skies</i>

41
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:39,790
<i>Flügel der Freiheit</i>

42
00:03:53,410 --> 00:03:58,290
"Forest of Giant Trees"
"The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 2"

43
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:09,500
How is your ODM gear, Armin?

44
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:14,830
It's all right. It unclasped properly,
so it doesn't seem to be broken.

45
00:04:14,830 --> 00:04:17,500
I see. That's good to hear.

46
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:21,330
But now what?
We only have one horse.

47
00:04:22,370 --> 00:04:26,410
If Jean's horse comes back,
all three of us can get moving again, but...

48
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:29,290
Damn, what's the deal?

49
00:04:29,290 --> 00:04:34,750
Reiner's horse came back;
why won't mine?

50
00:04:37,950 --> 00:04:42,000
And we can't afford
to stay here any longer...

51
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:47,540
Worst case scenario,
we'll have to leave someone here...

52
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:51,370
How will we choose
who that someone should be?

53
00:04:51,370 --> 00:04:53,910
Armin, because he's hurt?

54
00:04:53,910 --> 00:04:57,700
Reiner, because he's big
and would be hard to ride with?

55
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:01,660
Or should I go look
for my horse on foot?

56
00:05:03,370 --> 00:05:04,370
Damn!

57
00:05:04,370 --> 00:05:07,950
It's screwed up that we
even have to consider that!

58
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:10,540
The three of us just
managed to escape death!

59
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:13,580
This is one hell of a raw deal!

60
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,450
Armin.

61
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:34,330
Hey, Armin!

62
00:05:35,330 --> 00:05:38,290
I take it you're
still a bit mixed-up?

63
00:05:38,290 --> 00:05:39,580
Yeah.

64
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:41,910
I'm still a little dazed...

65
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:43,290
I see.

66
00:05:43,290 --> 00:05:45,830
Still, we need to decide now.

67
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:50,250
It's a difficult choice, but it looks
like one of us has to stay behind.

68
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,450
Wait!

69
00:05:54,870 --> 00:05:57,250
Let's fire a smoke signal first.

70
00:05:57,250 --> 00:05:59,250
If the formation
kept moving forward,

71
00:05:59,250 --> 00:06:02,580
Row 4, Squad 3
should be nearby now.

72
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,330
That was an emergency
smoke signal.

73
00:06:10,330 --> 00:06:14,000
I doubt it's enough to
get our point across, though.

74
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,830
Armin. We'll only
wait three minutes.

75
00:06:16,830 --> 00:06:18,910
By then, we need
to choose who'll stay--

76
00:06:18,910 --> 00:06:20,330
I'll stay.

77
00:06:21,450 --> 00:06:26,620
But, in exchange, I need
you to report about something.

78
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,450
Only to Commander Erwin, if possible.

79
00:06:28,450 --> 00:06:30,330
No, wait, Armin.

80
00:06:30,330 --> 00:06:33,250
You can report it yourself.

81
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:35,200
Someone's coming!

82
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:38,160
And they've brought two horses!

83
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:41,500
That's...

84
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,910
Christa!

85
00:06:45,910 --> 00:06:48,410
Guys! Are you okay?!

86
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:54,250
Huh? Hey, that's my horse!

87
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:57,540
Whoa, there.
Calm down, Buchwald!

88
00:06:57,540 --> 00:07:00,910
He came racing my way;
something must've really spooked him.

89
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,910
Did you guys fight a Titan?!

90
00:07:03,910 --> 00:07:05,250
Armin!

91
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:07,910
You're hurt! Are you all right?!

92
00:07:07,910 --> 00:07:09,910
Yes, more or less.

93
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:14,370
I'm impressed you willingly came
here after seeing that smoke signal.

94
00:07:14,370 --> 00:07:18,000
I happened to be nearby,
plus I'd found Jean's horse.

95
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:22,500
You have a way with horses, not to
mention a remarkable sense of virtue.

96
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,290
We owe you one.

97
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,450
I'm just glad.

98
00:07:27,450 --> 00:07:33,080
So very glad that the worst
didn't happen to you guys...

99
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,750
She's a god...

100
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:41,160
A goddess...

101
00:07:41,790 --> 00:07:43,410
I want to marry her...

102
00:07:44,250 --> 00:07:47,000
Well, we better
hurry back into formation!

103
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Oh, yeah! There should
be orders to retreat soon!

104
00:07:52,830 --> 00:07:57,000
Still, turning back not even
an hour after leaving the wall...

105
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,910
Things look way
grimmer than I thought.

106
00:07:59,910 --> 00:08:04,540
Plus, she's headed <i>away </i>from the
lead command squad for some reason.

107
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:05,950
She?

108
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:10,500
Green smoke signals?!

109
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:14,910
It sounds like the plan is to change
course but otherwise continue the operation.

110
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:17,580
Oh, no! They're not
ordering us to retreat?!

111
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:20,620
What the hell is
Commander Erwin thinking?!

112
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:26,750
All soldiers have the authority to
decide if the operation can't continue...

113
00:08:26,750 --> 00:08:29,750
Have the signals not
reached the command squad?!

114
00:08:29,750 --> 00:08:33,790
Whether or not they know, we only
have one option in this situation:

115
00:08:33,790 --> 00:08:35,870
defer to their judgment.

116
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:45,750
Smoke signals. Green.

117
00:08:45,750 --> 00:08:47,910
Oruo. You fire it.

118
00:08:47,910 --> 00:08:49,750
Understood, Sir!

119
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:53,160
It feels like we're making
smooth progress right now.

120
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,330
But...

121
00:08:55,330 --> 00:08:57,500
...I wonder how things <i>actually </i>are.

122
00:08:57,500 --> 00:09:00,620
I wonder if people have
already died on the front line...

123
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:02,250
Reporting, Sir!

124
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:03,950
It's an oral message!

125
00:09:03,950 --> 00:09:06,250
Right wing spotters decimated!

126
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:08,500
Detection network partially out!

127
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:12,120
Please pass this
message on to the left!

128
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:14,910
You heard him, Petra. Go.

129
00:09:14,910 --> 00:09:16,330
Yes, Sir!

130
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:19,620
The right wing?!

131
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:22,290
Isn't that where Armin is?

132
00:09:22,290 --> 00:09:27,660
Still, he and the others
are positioned closer to the center.

133
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:30,750
The Titans couldn't
have advanced that far in.

134
00:09:31,790 --> 00:09:33,620
Black signals?!

135
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:35,200
An Abnormal?!

136
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,330
Eren. You fire it.

137
00:09:37,330 --> 00:09:39,000
Y-Yes, Sir!

138
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,370
This is disgraceful.

139
00:09:41,370 --> 00:09:45,040
We've let them get
pretty deep inside the formation.

140
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:50,160
Just over there is a Titan...

141
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:53,120
Below that black smoke...

142
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:55,790
...someone is fighting?

143
00:10:07,290 --> 00:10:08,500
Damn!

144
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,330
Look down here...

145
00:10:10,950 --> 00:10:13,040
...you monster!

146
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,500
Now!

147
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,200
Three spots at once!

148
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:32,370
She seems pretty smart,
but she can't defend against them all!

149
00:10:32,370 --> 00:10:37,700
Cut her spine, ligaments,
or anywhere else that can stop her!

150
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:39,540
Attack!

151
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:42,580
So many are dead 'cause of you!

152
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:45,120
We're gonna torture you to death!

153
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,910
She jumped?!

154
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:07,790
L-Let go!

155
00:11:37,290 --> 00:11:38,700
Reporting takes priority!

156
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:43,410
I <i>have </i>to let
them know about that one!

157
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:51,950
An Abnormal?!

158
00:11:51,950 --> 00:11:53,500
This far in?!

159
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:54,700
Let's take it out!

160
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:57,950
We can't let it get any further in!

161
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:15,950
The right wing's been wiped out?!

162
00:12:15,950 --> 00:12:18,620
Then why aren't we retreating?!

163
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:21,200
"Row 3-1, Transport"
I don't know! Commander's orders!

164
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:23,160
"Row 3-1, Transport"
Just pass word on to the left!

165
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,540
What's the deal?

166
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:37,660
"Row 1-13: Spotting"
We've been going straight east for a while now.

167
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:40,500
Yes, and our destination
is the old city to the south...

168
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:44,450
"Row 1-5: Spotting"
At this rate, the formation's going to run right into it!

169
00:12:44,450 --> 00:12:45,750
Yeah.

170
00:12:45,750 --> 00:12:47,750
There it is.

171
00:12:47,750 --> 00:12:50,120
A forest of giant trees!

172
00:13:05,830 --> 00:13:08,910
It looks like Titans
have passed through here.

173
00:13:10,830 --> 00:13:13,250
The path is devoid of vegetation.

174
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:20,500
Even the wagons
could get through here.

175
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:22,620
Inform those behind us

176
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:26,290
that only the center wagon
defense squad is to enter the forest.

177
00:13:26,290 --> 00:13:27,700
Yes, Sir!

178
00:13:41,910 --> 00:13:43,790
Excuse me, Sir...

179
00:13:43,790 --> 00:13:47,290
It looks like the center rank
is taking that forest path.

180
00:13:47,290 --> 00:13:50,660
That means we'll
run smack into the forest.

181
00:13:51,910 --> 00:13:53,830
Then we go around.

182
00:13:53,830 --> 00:13:55,660
Y-Yes, Sir!

183
00:13:58,410 --> 00:13:59,660
Hey, now.

184
00:13:59,660 --> 00:14:02,580
What are we doing at
this sightseeing attraction?!

185
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:04,330
Now we're <i>really </i>straying

186
00:14:04,330 --> 00:14:07,660
from our original
destination and return point!

187
00:14:07,660 --> 00:14:09,580
I don't know...

188
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:12,910
I don't know, but this is
what Commander Erwin decided.

189
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:15,750
He seems to have
some plan in mind, but...

190
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:18,250
Plan? Are you kidding me?

191
00:14:18,250 --> 00:14:22,500
What, is he gonna throw a welcome
party for us rookies at this tourist spot?

192
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:24,910
No, I don't think so.

193
00:14:24,910 --> 00:14:26,870
That was a joke.

194
00:14:26,870 --> 00:14:30,620
Either way, we got
that giant broad after us.

195
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:35,620
Regardless of what plan he has,
we can't afford to stop here.

196
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:40,410
My guess is we're passing through
here on our way to somewhere else.

197
00:14:40,410 --> 00:14:42,410
All soldiers, halt!

198
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:48,750
All right! Listen up, rookies!

199
00:14:48,750 --> 00:14:51,250
We're now going to
take up intercept positions!

200
00:14:51,250 --> 00:14:53,620
Unsheathe and wait in the trees!

201
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:57,500
If any Titans try to enter the forest,
stop them with full force!

202
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,660
Huh?

203
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:00,580
Umm, Sir? Why would we need to--

204
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:02,790
Shut up and follow orders!

205
00:15:06,950 --> 00:15:08,450
You gotta be kidding me...

206
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:11,040
What the hell's happening?!

207
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,290
H-Hey.

208
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:19,200
It looks like only the
center rank went into the forest.

209
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,290
What does that mean
for the formation?

210
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:23,700
There is no formation anymore.

211
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:29,000
The forest is blocking us side squads,
so our only choice is to go around.

212
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,370
We've lost our spotting capabilities.

213
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:35,500
Why didn't we change course
and avoid the forest altogether?

214
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:38,830
Did Commander Erwin
misread his map or something?

215
00:15:38,830 --> 00:15:40,540
I don't know.

216
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:45,790
It's possible we got pushed here trying
to avoid the threat on the right side.

217
00:15:45,790 --> 00:15:47,200
Maybe.

218
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:58,750
This is insane...

219
00:15:58,750 --> 00:16:02,830
First we abandon our original
plan of establishing a logistics base...

220
00:16:02,830 --> 00:16:06,660
Then, instead of running home with
our tails between our legs like we should,

221
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:10,200
we go on a daring sightseeing tour...

222
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:13,040
And, if that wasn't enough,

223
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:16,540
now we're just supposed to stand here
and keep Titans out of the forest?

224
00:16:18,950 --> 00:16:23,200
Him and his idiotic orders...

225
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,620
He's gonna hear you.

226
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:28,500
And he doesn't even explain anything.
That's a new one to me.

227
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:32,700
But I doubt he's all that
calm on the inside either.

228
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,080
What do you mean?

229
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:38,870
Sometimes leaders get deemed incompetent
by their men in extreme situations

230
00:16:38,870 --> 00:16:43,000
and end up dying from
mysterious stab wounds to the back.

231
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,750
It's not that rare, is all I'm saying.

232
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:50,040
Jean... What are you thinking of doing?

233
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:52,250
Relax, will you?

234
00:16:52,250 --> 00:16:55,660
I'm just a little irritated at
this whole situation.

235
00:16:55,660 --> 00:17:00,250
I'm gonna follow orders, of course.

236
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:02,830
Keeping Titans out of the forest...

237
00:17:03,870 --> 00:17:07,750
You agree that's
what we should do too, right?

238
00:17:08,830 --> 00:17:11,410
You look like you know something.

239
00:17:11,410 --> 00:17:12,830
Uhh...

240
00:17:14,250 --> 00:17:16,120
5-meter Titan approaching!

241
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:26,660
Why did he bring the platoon here?

242
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:30,950
Just what is
Commander Erwin thinking?

243
00:17:30,950 --> 00:17:35,290
No, that's not right.
That isn't what I should be asking.

244
00:17:35,290 --> 00:17:38,120
What I should be asking is...

245
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:41,120
...what if the Female Titan
<i>is </i>pursuing Eren

246
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:45,330
and the commander is aware of that?

247
00:17:45,910 --> 00:17:47,330
Captain!

248
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:49,120
Captain Levi!

249
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,500
What?

250
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:53,700
"What?" This is a forest, Sir!

251
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:56,580
We have no way of detecting
approaching Titans this far in

252
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:59,040
with only the center rank!

253
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:01,620
Something seems to be on our right too.

254
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:05,950
How are we supposed to avoid
the Titans or protect the wagons now?!

255
00:18:05,950 --> 00:18:09,040
Quit whining about the obvious.

256
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:12,120
We can't do any
of those things anymore.

257
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:14,200
B-But why--?!

258
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:19,330
Take a good look around, Eren.
See all these absurdly huge trees?

259
00:18:20,950 --> 00:18:25,790
This is <i>the </i>perfect environment
for using omni-directional mobility gear.

260
00:18:25,790 --> 00:18:30,540
And use that middling
head of yours to think.

261
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:33,950
Use your brain for
once if you don't wanna die.

262
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:35,370
Yes, Sir!

263
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,750
I see...

264
00:18:37,750 --> 00:18:41,910
I'm still new to this; <i>that's </i>why
I don't understand the situation.

265
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:44,200
And he won't give me a simple answer

266
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:47,160
because I still need to learn for myself.

267
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:51,620
I bet that's how these
experts learned to fight, too.

268
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:56,120
Dammit, what are we doing here?

269
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:57,750
Seriously...

270
00:18:57,750 --> 00:19:01,540
What the hell's going on?

271
00:19:01,540 --> 00:19:02,790
Huh?!

272
00:19:02,790 --> 00:19:04,500
Don't tell me...?!

273
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:10,790
Don't tell me <i>no one</i>
knows what's going on?!

274
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:15,200
Not even Captain Levi?!

275
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:21,200
If my theory that the Female
Titan is after Eren is correct,

276
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:24,540
then there's only one
reason why we've come here.

277
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:28,450
Commander Erwin
intends to confront her here!

278
00:19:28,450 --> 00:19:29,870
Armin.

279
00:19:30,450 --> 00:19:36,000
Our orders are to
"keep Titans out of the forest," right?

280
00:19:37,620 --> 00:19:39,290
In other words...

281
00:19:39,290 --> 00:19:43,580
We don't need to
actually <i>fight </i>them...

282
00:19:43,580 --> 00:19:45,410
...right?

283
00:20:18,870 --> 00:20:21,910
--A black smoke signal?!
--From right behind us!

284
00:20:21,910 --> 00:20:25,080
Must be whatever's on the right!

285
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,700
Draw your swords.

286
00:20:29,870 --> 00:20:35,160
If it shows itself,
we'll only have a moment.

287
00:20:58,500 --> 00:20:59,910
Move!

288
00:21:14,290 --> 00:21:15,500
It's fast!

289
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:18,370
There's no way to
avoid it inside this forest!

290
00:21:18,370 --> 00:21:19,620
It's catching up!

291
00:21:19,620 --> 00:21:22,250
Captain! Let's switch to ODM!

292
00:21:22,250 --> 00:21:23,660
Captain!

293
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:27,580
You're not going anywhere!

294
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:29,120
Reinforcements from the rear!

295
00:21:44,910 --> 00:21:47,160
Captain! Give your orders!

296
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:49,950
Let's take it out! It's dangerous!

297
00:21:49,950 --> 00:21:51,910
<i>We </i>should take care of it!

298
00:21:53,370 --> 00:21:55,830
I'll cut it to shreds!

299
00:21:57,250 --> 00:22:00,660
Idiot! You walked
right into your own doom!

300
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:04,500
What you're chasing is
a team of expert Titan-killers!

301
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,830
Captain Levi!

302
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:10,830
Captain!

303
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:14,290
--Please give us orders!
--It's about to catch up to us!

304
00:22:14,290 --> 00:22:15,870
Let's take it out here!

305
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:19,790
That's why we entered
this forest! Isn't it, Captain?!

306
00:22:19,790 --> 00:22:22,120
Captain! Your orders!

307
00:22:24,910 --> 00:22:27,620
Everyone, cover your ears.

308
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:57,750
<i>If, by chance, I'm not me</i>

309
00:22:57,750 --> 00:23:03,000
<i>then who's to say that you're you?</i>

310
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:08,290
<i>Can you pick up the pieces of your heart</i>

311
00:23:08,290 --> 00:23:13,410
<i>that fell apart like a broken sand castle?</i>

312
00:23:13,410 --> 00:23:18,410
<i>The voice of someone calling out</i>

313
00:23:18,410 --> 00:23:22,500
<i>changed into ringing in my ears</i>

314
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:27,660
<i>It's as if time has stopped</i>

315
00:23:27,660 --> 00:23:30,450
<i>Now wake up</i>

316
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:35,750
<i>I made my way out of the deep darkness</i>

317
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:41,000
<i>I fled like a swift wind</i>

318
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:48,500
<i>We used to be like living corpses,</i>

319
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:50,540
<i>but now we head beyond the walls</i>

320
00:23:50,540 --> 00:23:52,580
<i>Let's meet again</i>

321
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:57,410
<i>in a place not on any map</i>

322
00:24:09,870 --> 00:24:14,290
The Female Titan makes chase,
leaving a bloodbath behind.

323
00:24:14,290 --> 00:24:19,330
Eren can only flee as he watches
his comrades die before his very eyes.

324
00:24:19,330 --> 00:24:21,830
Amid this, he's forced to make a decision.

325
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:23,370
"Bite"
"The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 3"
